# The survivors from screening, as a Taguchi array.
#
# Nine batches for four three-level factors, which a full factorial would want
# eighty-one for. That is the whole trade: main effects cheaply, interactions
# not at all.
#
# No `noise:` section here on purpose. Crossing the oven against the recipe
# asks a different question -- which recipe still tastes good when the oven is
# wrong -- and it is asked separately, and narrowly, in cookies-robust.tgu.
# Mixing the two questions into one array means neither gets nine clean rows,
# and `analyze` reads a crossed file as control settings when its run ids are
# really inner x outer pairs. It refuses that file now; this one is the design
# it is meant to read.
factors:
  butter: 0.5, 0.75, 1.0
  temp: 350, 375, 400
  time: 9, 11, 13
  flour: 2.0, 2.375, 2.75

array: L9
